      "text": "Given the equation \\(x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0\\), we can rearrange it to find an expression for \\(x^{2017}\\):\n\n\\[x^{2017} = 2x - 1.\\]\n\nWe need to find the value of the sum \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\). This is a geometric series with the first term \\(a = 1\\) and common ratio \\(r = x\\). The number of terms in the series is 2017. The sum \\(S_n\\) of a geometric series is given by the formula:\n\n\\[S_n = a \\frac{r^n - 1}{r - 1}.\\]\n\nIn our case, \\(a = 1\\), \\(r = x\\), and \\(n = 2017\\), so the sum is:\n\n\\[S_{2017} = \\frac{x^{2017} - 1}{x - 1}.\\]\n\nFrom the given equation, we know \\(x^{2017} = 2x - 1\\). Substituting this into the sum formula, we get:\n\n\\[S_{2017} = \\frac{(2x - 1) - 1}{x - 1} = \\frac{2x - 2}{x - 1} = \\frac{2(x - 1)}{x - 1} = 2.\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the sum \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
