      "text": "To solve the given problem, we start by analyzing the polynomial equation:\n\n\\[\nx^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0\n\\]\n\nFirst, we rearrange the equation to isolate the polynomial expression on one side:\n\n\\[\nx^{2017} = 2x - 1\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the value of the sum:\n\n\\[\nx^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\n\\]\n\nThis is a geometric series with the first term \\(a = x\\) and common ratio \\(r = x\\). The sum \\(S\\) of the first \\(n+1\\) terms of a geometric series is given by:\n\n\\[\nS = \\frac{a(r^{n+1} - 1)}{r - 1}\n\\]\n\nIn our case, the series has \\(2017\\) terms, so \\(n = 2016\\). Therefore, the sum is:\n\n\\[\nS = \\frac{x(x^{2017} - 1)}{x - 1}\n\\]\n\nWe already know from the rearranged equation that \\(x^{2017} = 2x - 1\\). Substituting this into the sum formula, we get:\n\n\\[\nS = \\frac{x((2x - 1) - 1)}{x - 1} = \\frac{x(2x - 2)}{x - 1} = \\frac{2x(x - 1)}{x - 1}\n\\]\n\nFor \\(x \\neq 1\\), the \\(x - 1\\) terms cancel out:\n\n\\[\nS = 2x\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of the sum \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2x}\n\\]",
